  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The population $Z(t)$ of zebras in a certain nature reserve is given by $Z(t)=10\\,000\\cdot (1.2)^{t}$, where $t$ is the time in years since the reserve was opened. How many zebras will be in the reserve after $4$ years?",
  "worked_solution": "To get the number of zebras after $4$ years, we evaluate the function at $t=4.$ Substituting $t=4$ into the function $Z(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & =10\\,000\\cdot (1.2)^{(4)} \\\\  & =10\\,000\\cdot 2.073\\,6 \\\\  & =20\\,736.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $4$ years, there will be $20\\,736$ zebras in the nature reserve.",
